WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.239
A functioning city depends on work
most of us never see.

2
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:11.144
Beneath our streets, workers maintain the systems
that carry wastewater away.

3
00:00:13.717 --> 00:00:17.122
But keeping a city running should not come
at the cost of their safety.

4
00:00:21.617 --> 00:00:26.152
Industrial robots are automatically controlled,
reprogrammable, multipurpose manipulators,

5
00:00:26.152 --> 00:00:31.255
programmable in three or more axes for industrial
automation.

6
00:00:31.255 --> 00:00:35.791
Typical applications include material handling,
assembly and welding.

7
00:00:41.117 --> 00:00:45.507
Service robots perform useful tasks for people or
equipment.

8
00:00:45.507 --> 00:00:50.874
IFR distinguishes consumer robots, intended for
use without professional training, from

9
00:00:50.874 --> 00:00:54.289
professional service robots, intended for trained
operators.

10
00:00:55.217 --> 00:00:59.167
In 2015, United Nations member states adopted
the 2030 Agenda,

11
00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:03.197
including seventeen Sustainable Development Goals.

12
00:01:03.967 --> 00:01:05.067
No Poverty

13
00:01:05.067 --> 00:01:06.267
Zero Hunger

14
00:01:06.267 --> 00:01:07.800
Good Health and Well-being

15
00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.333
Quality Education

16
00:01:09.333 --> 00:01:10.667
Gender Equality

17
00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:12.600
Clean Water and Sanitation

18
00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.500
Affordable and Clean Energy

19
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:16.833
Decent Work and Economic Growth

20
00:01:16.833 --> 00:01:19.767
Industry, Innovation and Infrastructure

21
00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:21.467
Reduced Inequalities

22
00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:23.933
Sustainable Cities and Communities

23
00:01:23.933 --> 00:01:26.433
Responsible Consumption and Production

24
00:01:26.433 --> 00:01:27.600
Climate Action

25
00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:28.967
Life Below Water

26
00:01:28.967 --> 00:01:30.100
Life on Land

27
00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:33.067
Peace, Justice and Strong Institutions

28
00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:35.133
And Partnerships for the Goals

29
00:01:36.083 --> 00:01:37.720
These goals are interconnected.

30
00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:43.447
Together, they ask us to judge technological
progress by whether it improves people's lives

31
00:01:43.447 --> 00:01:45.083
and protects the planet.

32
00:01:45.383 --> 00:01:49.645
Let us look at how robots can contribute to these
goals in practice.

33
00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:55.060
Agricultural robots can automate harvesting,
helping reduce labour bottlenecks and crop

34
00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:55.524
losses.

35
00:01:55.524 --> 00:02:01.098
Their contribution to Zero Hunger depends on
affordability and access for farmers.

36
00:02:01.417 --> 00:02:06.625
Surgical robots translate a surgeon's movements
into controlled instrument actions for tasks

37
00:02:06.625 --> 00:02:07.927
such as suturing.

38
00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:11.834
They assist the clinician rather than replace
clinical judgement.

39
00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:15.854
Sorting robots separate recyclable materials for
recovery.

40
00:02:15.854 --> 00:02:21.675
Their contribution to responsible consumption
depends on sorting accuracy and effective

41
00:02:21.675 --> 00:02:22.733
downstream recycling.

42
00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:25.900
This is Jason, a sewer worker.

43
00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:31.599
In confined spaces, workers can face contaminated
waste, dangerous gases and difficult

44
00:02:31.599 --> 00:02:32.549
physical conditions.

45
00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:37.382
If the cleaning must happen below ground, does
the worker have to go down too?

46
00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:43.843
Bandicoot offers a different approach: keep the
operator above ground and send a robotic

47
00:02:43.843 --> 00:02:45.948
cleaning unit into the manhole.

48
00:02:45.948 --> 00:02:51.421
NITI Aayog's 2025 Bandicoot case study reports
that over three thousand sanitation workers

49
00:02:51.421 --> 00:02:53.105
have received robot-operation training.

50
00:02:53.417 --> 00:02:58.858
From the surface, the operator uses a control
station to direct the equipment as the working

51
00:02:58.858 --> 00:03:00.559
unit is lowered into position.

52
00:03:02.617 --> 00:03:07.353
Cameras provide visual feedback, while gas
sensors help identify atmospheric hazards.

53
00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:12.951
The operator uses this information to guide the
cleaning arm from the surface.

54
00:03:13.283 --> 00:03:18.892
The arm transfers debris into a collection
bucket, reducing direct human exposure.

55
00:03:18.892 --> 00:03:24.033
Safe deployment still depends on access,
equipment maintenance and trained operation.

56
00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:29.618
The collected material is brought to the surface
and transferred into a waste container for

57
00:03:29.618 --> 00:03:30.321
onward handling.

58
00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:41.102
This connects with several goals: SDG 6 through
sanitation maintenance; SDG 3 through reduced

59
00:03:41.102 --> 00:03:45.781
hazardous exposure; and SDG 9 through innovation
in infrastructure maintenance.

60
00:03:46.083 --> 00:03:52.749
Our focus is SDG 8, particularly Target 8.8:
protecting labour rights and promoting safe and

61
00:03:52.749 --> 00:03:55.416
secure working environments for all workers.

62
00:03:55.717 --> 00:03:58.924
For Jason, this means learning a new role.

63
00:03:58.924 --> 00:04:03.735
Training helps him operate the equipment,
understand its limitations and work safely.

64
00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:07.279
But the transition also raises an ethical
challenge.

65
00:04:07.279 --> 00:04:13.332
Workers without equal access to training may be
left behind, facing job losses or lower

66
00:04:13.332 --> 00:04:13.736
incomes.

67
00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:18.449
Deployment should include paid training, income
protection and worker participation.

68
00:04:18.449 --> 00:04:23.727
Success should be assessed through fewer
hazardous entries and injuries, alongside secure

69
00:04:23.727 --> 00:04:26.366
employment and respect for labour rights.

70
00:04:26.683 --> 00:04:30.945
The benefits of automation should reach the
people whose work it changes.

71
00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:35.019
A functioning city depends on work we rarely see.

72
00:04:35.019 --> 00:04:37.679
Robots can help make that work safer.

73
00:04:37.679 --> 00:04:42.998
Sustainable development means ensuring that the
people doing it can also enjoy better lives.
